== VRChat Wiki ==
I have been here since this wiki started and I am one of the maintainers on [[VRCWiki:Team]]. Full paper trail at [https://wiki.vrchat.com/wiki/Special:Contributions/Usr_40be82e7-f7d5-4548-b314-3fc7b26d22ee Special:Contributions].

Edit count or line change count are bad metrics. A page written from scratch and a fixed typo both count as one edit. A rewrite eats an afternoon. A lot of my heavy lifting is template plumbing and translation units that never surface as prose.

What I actually do: platform documentation such as [[Getting Started]], [[Instances]], [[Groups]], [[Menus]], [[Social]], [[OSC]], [[Community:OSC Resources]], [[Avatar Dynamics]], [[Items]] and [[Badges]], several of which started on my keyboard — including the OSC and OSC Resources pages. German localization is my largest single share of edits — German page versions, plus proofreading on Crowdin for VRChat itself. I also write the community tooling pages nobody else wants to own: [[Community:VRCX]], [[Community:Vrc-get]], [[Community:ALCOM]], [[Community:Manage VRChat]], [[VRC Quick Launcher]]. The tools everyone uses and nobody documents.

[[Community:Potentially Upcoming Features]] is my most edited page. It started as a dump for datamined and pre-announcement findings, then got renamed and restructured after a long argument about where that kind of information belongs. Seasonal events, exhibitions, dance and photography land here too, including [[Community:VRDancing]] and [[Community:VR Photography Exhibitions]].

=== Automated contributions ===
Not everything I contribute is typed by hand. I run bots on [https://vrchat.com/home/user/usr_bbbda87a-b179-41d3-bdcf-6fa732bd4c19 HackebeinsBot], the account the Music Truck project used in-game before it got a second job. Those edits are data feeds from other sources, so manual work stays reserved for things a bot cannot do yet. Public list at [https://wiki.vrchat.com/wiki/Special:Contributions/Usr_bbbda87a-b179-41d3-bdcf-6fa732bd4c19 Special:Contributions].

The bot keeps world data pages behind the infoboxes up to date — visits, favorites, heat — plus the VPM package version summary and the per-package version templates. It also syncs [[Template:Version|client build metadata]] for Steam, Meta Quest, Pico Store, Google Play and Viveport, and creator tool versions for the [[VRChat Creator Companion]] and [[VRC Quick Launcher]]. Marketplace shelves and paid avatar listing pages are in scope too; those just show up less often than the world and build syncs.

