=== Object Tracking ===
[[File:Hackebein_object_tracking_wip.jpg|thumb|right|WIP screenshot of a tracker in VRChat]]
Track your real-world objects and bring them into VRChat, with any tracker SteamVR and OpenVR support. Cups, chairs, poles, aerial hoops (lyra), guitars, decks, pets, cameras, or your entire room. Communities are forming around exactly this <ref>https://vrchat.com/home/group/grp_b9665434-bcce-4260-bbdc-ae3b7c48edf0 - TRACKD.6559</ref>.

It began in mid-2022 with one goal: make my pole spin in VRChat at the speed it spins in my flat. One axis was enough for about a week. It now does full six degrees of freedom. Demos live on my social media, like this [https://x.com/Hackebein/status/1817729114142343460 one].

It is also the rig behind my performance art. Aerial hoop, pole and swinging bench, in VR, on the same trackers.

The desktop application ships on [https://store.steampowered.com/app/3140770 Steam] as an auto-updating build. The avatar side installs from my VPM listing. Companion packages cover an aerial hoop, a simple dance pole example and the tracking host.

